------------------------------------------------------------------------
vectcut-api/
  Based on VectCutAPI by sun-guannan
  https://github.com/sun-guannan/VectCutAPI  (commit cfa4779a52f1dc59a56d90cc5868778eb50c6a97)
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see vectcut-api/LICENSE).

  Changes made in this repository (each modified file carries a header notice):
  - web_preview.py, capcut_server.py: the Windows-only desktop_companion import
    is optional, so the server starts on macOS.
  - save_draft_impl.py: drafts are written straight into the local CapCut drafts
    folder (macOS and Windows), the folder is renamed to project_name, and
    draft_meta_info.json is rewritten (the template carried the original
    author's paths and ids).
  - add_effect_impl.py: effect parameters are passed in order (they were
    reversed, and an effect without parameters crashed).
  - add_audio_track.py, capcut_server.py: audio fade_in / fade_out.
  - add_image_impl.py, capcut_server.py: image rotation.
  - media_analysis.py (new): local Whisper transcription saved next to the video,
    pause detection, pause-free assembly with one shared media material, and
    subtitles generated from the transcript that follow the edit.
  - capcut_server.py: routes for the above; add_video records clip placement.
  - camera_moves.py (new): virtual camera moves from keyframes (sampled on every
    clip a move overlaps) and CapCut effects; /camera_moves and /add_camera_move.
    Moves compose with existing and pending keyframes (or replace / refuse), never
    duplicate timestamps, squeeze into short ranges, offer easing presets, and
    scale effect strength with intensity.
  - save_draft_impl.py: media under ~/Movies is referenced in place (CapCut is
    sandboxed and can read that folder); a file used by many clips is copied once.
  - downloader.py: local files are cloned copy-on-write on macOS (APFS).
  - save_draft_impl.py, capcut_server.py: safe saving. project names are
    validated (no '.', '..' or separators), the draft is built in a staging folder
    and swapped in, an existing folder is moved to backups instead of deleted,
    projects not saved from the same draft need overwrite, replacing a project is
    refused while CapCut is open, and failed copies are reported as failures.
  - add_text_impl.py, add_audio_track.py: an unknown animation or audio effect name
    is an error (it was silently ignored).
  - add_video_keyframe_impl.py, pyJianYingDraft/track.py: a keyframe with no clip at
    its time is an error when added; a batch is validated before any is queued;
    pending keyframes that cannot be applied raise instead of being dropped.
  - create_draft.py, capcut_server.py: the requested fps (24/25/30/50/60) is applied
    and returned with the size (it was ignored).
  - draft_store.py (new), create_draft.py, capcut_server.py, save_draft_impl.py: drafts
    are stored in SQLite and survive a restart; routes that change a draft run under
    a per-draft lock and roll back on failure; an unknown draft_id is an error (no
    more implicit creation).
  - existing_project.py (new), save_draft_impl.py, capcut_server.py: open a project
    made in CapCut (/open_project) and add tracks to it; the original timeline is
    written back unchanged in all its copies, after a full backup, and only if the
    project did not change since it was opened and CapCut is closed. list_projects
    flags real projects.
  - media_analysis.py: subtitles are placed from the clips on the timeline instead
    of an in-memory list.
  - util.py: Windows asset paths built on macOS no longer double the drive separator.
  - draft_profiles.py: the canvas ratio is adjusted only when the content has a
    canvas_config (one was invented otherwise).
  - requirements.lock.txt, requirements-whisper-mlx.lock.txt (new): exact versions.
  - placement.py (new), pyJianYingDraft/script_file.py, draft_store.py: an item that
    would overlap on its track goes to the first free track like it (auto_track).
  - music.py (new), capcut_server.py: /add_background_music (loop, fades, ducking under
    the voice from its transcript) and /timeline.
  - camera_moves.json (new): camera move names and descriptions, read by both
    camera_moves.py and the MCP server.
  - media_analysis.py, capcut_server.py: /transcribe can return one page of blocks
    (no word timings) instead of the whole transcript.
  - kit_auth.py (new), capcut_server.py: GET /health identifies the backend; every
    other request needs the shared token. settings/local.py: CAPCUT_PORT override.
  - downloader.py: remote downloads are http(s) only, size-capped, never left
    partial, and a failure is an error.
  - capcut_server.py: the web preview routes are off unless CAPCUT_ENABLE_PREVIEW=1;
    requests with a non-loopback Host or Origin are refused.
  - tests/test_save_draft_local_paths.py: never writes into the real CapCut folder;
    tests/test_save_draft_safety.py, test_media_analysis.py, test_no_false_success.py,
    test_draft_store.py, test_existing_project.py, test_camera_moves.py,
    test_downloader.py, test_placement_and_music.py, test_catalog_and_paging.py,
    test_contracts.py (new).
  - pyJianYingDraft/script_file.py: import_srt crashed when no font was given.
  - The upstream mcp-server/ folder (a copy of the project below) is not included.

